{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1662","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. European Trip"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The map of Europe can be represented by a set of $$$n$$$ cities, numbered from $$$1$$$ through $$$n$$$, which are connected by $$$m$$$ bidirectional roads, each of which connects two distinct cities. A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"trip"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of length $$$k$$$ is a sequence of $$$k+1$$$ cities $$$v_1, v_2, \\ldots, v_{k+1}$$$ such that there is a road connecting each consecutive pair $$$v_i$$$, $$$v_{i+1}$$$ of cities, for all $$$1 \\le i \\le k$$$. A "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"special trip"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is a trip that does not use the same road twice in a row, i.e., a sequence of $$$k+1$$$ cities $$$v_1, v_2, \\ldots, v_{k+1}$$$ such that it forms a trip and $$$v_i \\neq v_{i + 2}$$$, for all $$$1 \\le i \\le k - 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Given an integer $$$k$$$, compute the number of distinct special trips of length $$$k$$$ which begin and end in the same city. Since the answer might be large, give the answer modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains three integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$3 \\le n \\le 100$$$, $$$1 \\le m \\le n(n - 1) / 2$$$, $$$1 \\le k \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of cities, the number of roads and the length of trips to consider."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the following $$$m$$$ lines contains a pair of distinct integers $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$ ($$$1 \\le a, b \\le n$$$) — each pair represents a road connecting cities $$$a$$$ and $$$b$$$. It is guaranteed that the roads are distinct (i.e., each pair of cities is connected by at most one road)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the number of special trips of length $$$k$$$ which begin and end in the same city, modulo $$$998\\,244\\,353$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 5 2\n4 1\n2 3\n3 1\n4 3\n2 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4 5 3\n1 3\n4 2\n4 1\n2 1\n3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n12\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8 20 12\n4 3\n6 7\n5 7\n8 2\n8 3\n3 1\n4 7\n8 5\n5 4\n3 5\n7 1\n5 1\n7 8\n3 2\n4 2\n5 2\n1 4\n4 8\n3 6\n4 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n35551130\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"first sample"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", we are looking for special trips of length $$$2$$$, but since we cannot use the same road twice once we step away from a city we cannot go back, so the answer is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"second sample"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", we have the following $$$12$$$ special trips of length $$$3$$$ which begin and end in the same city: $$$(1, 2, 4, 1)$$$, $$$(1, 3, 4, 1)$$$, $$$(1, 4, 2, 1)$$$, $$$(1, 4, 3, 1)$$$, $$$(2, 1, 4, 2)$$$, $$$(2, 4, 1, 2)$$$, $$$(3, 1, 4, 3)$$$, $$$(3, 4, 1, 3)$$$, $$$(4, 1, 3, 4)$$$, $$$(4, 3, 1, 4)$$$, $$$(4, 1, 2, 4)$$$, and $$$(4, 2, 1, 4)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1662C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1662/problem/C"}